Subject: MQS 1.3 SIT – BICoE Observations and Remaining Validation

Hi Team,

Sharing the current BICoE view of the MQS 1.3 SIT testing and the remaining observations we would like to close/understand before completing the lower-environment testing.

What is working

The earlier issue where core_request was replayed into the BICoE Event Hub, although it belongs to the QWD/Working Data flow, has now been retested in SIT and is working as expected. The replay is now respecting the intended BICoE/QWD routing.

Observation 1 – Blob replay completeness – needs confirmation

For the controlled set of 10 MQS IDs confirmed as reprocessed from Blob, BICoE was able to identify 9/10 records in the Event Hub.

The remaining MQS ID still needs end-to-end tracing to understand why it is not visible on the BICoE side, despite being reported as processed from the Blob batch. Could Mule/Ash please help confirm the path/status of this record?

Observation 2 – Timeout/replay duplicate behaviour – request to validate in SIT

Initially, we considered validating this further during performance testing because the ACK-timeout condition could not be reproduced consistently for BICoE. However, after reviewing the patterns already present in Production, I think it would be better to validate this in a controlled lower-environment scenario if possible.

We are seeing a few variations in Production:

Same-day replay: the same message can arrive multiple times on the same day — in some samples approximately 10 times. BICoE's existing deduplication is able to handle this pattern.
Cross-day replay: the original message is received on one day and the replayed copy arrives on a subsequent day with a new Event Hub enqueuedTime. This is more concerning because the existing BICoE deduplication does not necessarily identify it as the same event, allowing duplicates to progress into DLT/Silverish.
Same MQSQuoteId + messageType with different quoteStep: we have also identified Production samples where the same Quote/Message Type combination appears with more than one quoteStep. This can similarly bypass the current deduplication behaviour.

The cross-day scenario is the main reason we would like Observation 2 exercised in SIT rather than relying only on performance testing. We need to understand the expected Mule/MQS behaviour when an Event Hub publish succeeds but the acknowledgement times out, the message subsequently enters Blob, and replay occurs later.

Could Mule/Ash please confirm whether we can reproduce this in a controlled manner in SIT and validate what happens to the original and replayed message? I am happy to provide additional Production samples covering the different patterns above if useful.

Observation 3 – STOP-QUOTE coverage – lower priority / non-blocking

STOP-QUOTE was not generated in the current automation test data, so we could not validate a STOP-QUOTE flowing through Blob replay.

We understand this requires a more specific test-data scenario and therefore don't see it as a release blocker at this stage. However, considering the Production patterns we are now reviewing, it would be useful for the Mule/MQS team to confirm whether there is any message-type-specific behaviour around STOP-QUOTE/replay that requires further investigation.

So from the BICoE side, the main remaining focus is Observation 1 (9/10 replay completeness) and particularly Observation 2 (controlled timeout/replay behaviour). Observation 3 can remain a lower-priority coverage item unless the upstream investigation identifies a specific risk.

